# Allow-list gitignore: /* blocks every TOP-LEVEL path; ! re-allows with a reason.
# (A bare * would also block files inside allowed directories; directory
# contents are governed by their own /* rules below where needed.)

/*

!/.gitignore
# Why: the allow-list itself must be versioned so every clone agrees on what is source.

!/project.yml
# Why: XcodeGen source of truth; pikicam.xcodeproj is generated from it.

!/.swiftlint.yml
# Why: strict lint is a gate; the config must not drift per machine.
!/.swift-format
# Why: same for formatting.

!/pikicam
# Why: the app is the product — the whole subtree is source.

!/pikicamTests
# Why: unit tests mirror the app tree.
pikicamTests/Fixtures/*.DNG
# Why not: multi-MB device captures; SHA-registered outside git.

!/pikicamUITests
# Why: the one real-pipeline smoke suite (device).

!/scripts
# Why: verification and oracle scripts are part of the product contract.

!/pikicam.xcodeproj
# Why: generated but committed so a clean clone passes the determinism diff
# and builds without xcodegen; xcuserdata stays blocked.

!/docs
/docs/*
# Why: the docs directory holds working material that stays local; each
# shipped doc is allowed individually below.
!/docs/DIAGNOSIS.md
# Why: the recorded failures the rebuild fixes; evidence for every cut.
!/docs/WALK.md
# Why: the acceptance walk definition and the measured budget numbers.
!/docs/SKIN.md
# Why: the token table and every deliberate HIG deviation.

!/README.md
# Why: front door + inversion documentation.
!/AGENTS.md
# Why: the operating contract for coding agents.

!/fixtures
/fixtures/*
# Why: fixture payloads are device-specific multi-MB DNGs (blocked), but the
# SHA register and probe JSON are reproducibility evidence.
!/fixtures/device/SHA256SUMS.txt
!/fixtures/device/probe-results.json

.DS_Store
